  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 11 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nBuilt in the 1970s and thoughtfully extended in the 1980s, this exceptional property occupies a peaceful position off a tree-lined boulevard on Glendowie's sought-after eastern coastal peninsula. Offered for sale for the very first time by its original owners, the home has been the setting for treasured family memories and everyday living for over five decades. Immaculately presented and meticulously maintained, it enjoys an enviable location close to sandy beaches, estuary boat ramps, public transport and the ever-popular Churchill Park.\r\nA tranquil water feature welcomes you to this two-storey, 191m² (approx.) cedar and concrete block residence, beautifully positioned within established, landscaped grounds. Tastefully decorated throughout, the home offers generous living spaces with seamless indoor-outdoor flow from both the spacious dining room and main lounge. A circular patio, manicured lawn and charming fishpond create a private, walled courtyard, providing an idyllic setting for relaxation and entertaining. The open-plan kitchen retains the warmth and character of its original timber flooring and offers excellent cabinetry and a substantial walk-in pantry. A second separate lounge provides flexibility as a family retreat, media room or home office. Three ground-floor bedrooms are serviced by a stylish tiled bathroom with a separate bath, shower and toilet. Upstairs, the spacious master suite offers a peaceful sanctuary, enhanced by high raked ceilings, abundant natural light, a walk-in wardrobe, ensuite and adjoining study, with potential to further expand the wardrobe space. Practical storage is plentiful, including a garden shed and secure storage within the carport.\r\nSet on a flat, freehold 690m² (approx.) section, the property offers beautifully maintained outdoor spaces with plenty of room for children and pets to enjoy. With coastal walkways, parks and recreational facilities close by, along with zoning for highly regarded Glendowie College and Churchill Park School, and Sacred Heart College also close by, this much-loved home presents an outstanding opportunity for families and downsizers alike. A rare chance to secure a cherished property in one of Glendowie's most desirable neighbourhoods, ready for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
